# ⚠️ CRITICAL UPDATES NEEDED

---

# 1. 🚨 REMOVE DUAL ITEM SYSTEM CONFUSION

## Current Problem

You currently have BOTH:

* `items`
* `shop_items`

This creates architecture confusion. 

You are mixing:

* marketplace product catalog
* shop-owned products

This will eventually create:

* duplicate logic
* duplicate APIs
* variant mismatch
* reporting confusion

---

## Needed Update

### Choose ONE structure.

Recommended:

```text
demo_items → items
```

Where:

* `demo_items` = templates
* `items` = actual shop-owned products

Remove:

```sql
shop_items
```

---

## Why?

Because currently:

| Table      | Purpose              |
| ---------- | -------------------- |
| items      | actual products      |
| shop_items | also actual products |

That is overlapping responsibility.

---

## Better Structure

```text
demo_items
    ↓ clone
items
    ↓
item_sell_config
    ↓
item_variants
```

Much cleaner.

---

## Merit

* Cleaner APIs
* Easier joins
* Better analytics
* Less duplicate logic

---

## Risk

Migration required now before production.

---

# 2. 🚨 ADD “CONFIG PREVIEW” BEFORE SAVE

## Current Problem

Shop owners will not understand:

* manual
* packed
* dynamic
* portion

Even if backend is correct. 

---

## Needed Update

Before final save:

Show live preview:

```text
Customer will see:

[ 500g ] [ 1kg ]
Price updates automatically
```

OR

```text
Customer selects:
Small Chicken
Estimated: ₹240–₹280
```

---

## Why Critical?

Your entire system depends on variant understanding.

Without preview:

* wrong configurations
* pricing confusion
* support burden

---

## Merit

* Prevents seller mistakes
* Reduces abandoned orders

---

## Risk

Requires extra frontend work.

But absolutely worth it.

---

# 3. 🚨 LOCK TECHNICAL FIELDS HARDER

## Current Problem

Shopkeepers can potentially create structurally inconsistent items.

Example:

* Vegetables with litre units
* Dynamic pricing for stationery

You already planned category restrictions. 

But enforcement is not fully defined.

---

## Needed Update

Backend validation must enforce:

```text
Category
    ↓
Allowed Unit Groups
    ↓
Allowed Sell Modes
```

NOT frontend-only validation.

---

## Add Database-Level Constraints

Example logic:

```text
Vegetables:
✔ weight
✔ portion

❌ volume
❌ dynamic (optional)
```

---

## Merit

* Prevents catalog corruption
* Keeps UI predictable

---

## Risk

Slightly more backend complexity.

Necessary complexity.

---

# 4. 🚨 VARIANT GENERATION SHOULD BE SEMI-AUTOMATIC

## Current Problem

Manual variant entry will become painful.

Especially for:

* grocery
* vegetables
* nuts

---

## Needed Update

When seller selects:

```text
Sell mode = manual
Base unit = gram
```

System auto-generates:

```text
250g
500g
1kg
2kg
```

Seller can:

* disable
* edit
* reorder

---

## Merit

* Faster onboarding
* Consistent catalog
* Better UX

---

## Risk

Some shops need unusual sizes.

Allow custom additions.

---

# 5. 🚨 ADD “ITEM HEALTH VALIDATION”

## Current Problem

Your system allows incomplete but technically valid items.

Example:

* no image
* no variants
* no default variant
* price missing

These silently break UI.

---

## Needed Update

Add item completeness scoring.

Example:

| Check          | Status |
| -------------- | ------ |
| Image uploaded | ✅      |
| Price set      | ✅      |
| Variant exists | ❌      |

Final status:

```text
Item incomplete
Cannot publish
```

---

## Merit

* Prevents broken storefronts
* Better customer trust

---

## Risk

More validation logic.

But this saves huge operational headaches later.

---

